{"name":"Morning Haze","hex":"#e0e8ed","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"morning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The early part of the day, especially from midnight to noon. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The early part of anything."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good morning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morning"},{"term":"haze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Very fine solid particles (smoke, dust) or liquid droplets (moisture) suspended in the air, slightly limiting visibility.","A reduction of transparency of a clear gas or liquid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be or become hazy, or thick with haze."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Morning","blocks":[{"text":"Morning is either the period from sunrise to noon, or the period from midnight to noon. In the first definition it is preceded by the twilight period of dawn, and there are no exact times for when morning begins because it can vary according to one's latitude, and the hours of daytime at each time of year. However, morning strictly ends at noon, when afternoon starts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg/330px-Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morning","wikidata":"Q7722"},{"title":"Haze","blocks":[{"text":"Haze is traditionally an atmospheric phenomenon in which dust, smoke, and other dry particulates suspended in air obscure visibility and the clarity of the sky. The World Meteorological Organization manual of codes includes a classification of particulates causing horizontal obscuration into categories of fog, ice fog, steam fog, mist, haze, smoke, volcanic ash, dust, sand, and snow. Sources for particles that cause haze include farming, traffic, industry, windy weather, volcanic activity and wildfires.\nSeen from afar and depending on the direction of view with respect to the Sun, haze may appear brownish or bluish, while mist tends to be bluish grey instead. Whereas haze often is considered a phenomenon occurring in dry air, mist formation is a phenomenon in saturated, humid air. However, haze particles may act as condensation nuclei that leads to the subsequent vapor condensation and formation of mist droplets; such forms of haze are known as \"wet haze\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/MosqueinAbuja.jpg/330px-MosqueinAbuja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haze","wikidata":"Q643546"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/500px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/1280px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/500px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Comet Ison at dawn, with Mercury at left","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AComet_ison.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg/500px-Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg/1280px-Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg/500px-Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Haze over the Mojave Desert from a brush fire in Santa Barbara, California, seen as the Sun descends on the 2016 June solstice, allows the Sun to be photographed without a filter.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStriped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg/500px-Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg/1280px-Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg/500px-Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Haze as smoke pollution over the Mojave from fires in the Inland Empire, June 2016, demonstrates the loss of contrast to the Sun, and the landscape in general.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/500px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/1280px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/500px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAir_pollution3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Sun_during_sunset.jpg/500px-Sun_during_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Sun_during_sunset.jpg/1280px-Sun_during_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Sun_during_sunset.jpg/500px-Sun_during_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The sun viewed directly through a thick haze of atmospheric dust in Meknes, Morocco","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASun_during_sunset.jpg"}],"sounds":{"morning":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/En-uk-morning.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b9/En-uk-morning.ogg/En-uk-morning.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9b/En-us-morning.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9b/En-us-morning.ogg/En-us-morning.ogg.mp3"}],"haze":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0d/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-haze.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0d/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-haze.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-haze.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0d/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-haze.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-haze.wav.ogg"}]}}}